## 6️⃣ Data Layer – Fetching & Caching

### 6.1 Using React Query

```tsx
import { useQuery } from '@tanstack/react-query';
import axios from 'axios';

export const useProducts = () => {
  return useQuery(['products'], async () => {
    const { data } = await axios.get('/api/products');
    return data;
  });
};
```

### 6.2 API Routes (pages/api/products.ts)

```ts
import type { NextApiRequest, NextApiResponse } from 'next';
import { prisma } from '@/lib/prisma';

export default async function handler(req: NextApiRequest, res: NextApiResponse) {
  const products = await prisma.product.findMany();
  res.json(products);
}
```

> **Tip:** If you’re using a headless CMS (e.g., Strapi, Contentful), replace the Prisma call with the CMS SDK.

---

## 7️⃣ Authentication & Authorization

| Library | Use‑case |
|---------|----------|
| **NextAuth.js** | OAuth (Google, GitHub), email/password, JWT |
| **Auth.js** | Server‑less auth, JWT, session storage |
| **Supabase Auth** | Full‑stack auth + database |

**Example (NextAuth)**

```ts
// pages/api/auth/[...nextauth].ts
import NextAuth from 'next-auth';
import GoogleProvider from 'next-auth/providers/google';

export default NextAuth({
  providers: [
    GoogleProvider({
      clientId: process.env.GOOGLE_ID!,
      clientSecret: process.env.GOOGLE_SECRET!,
    }),
  ],
  callbacks: {
    async session({ session, token }) {
      session.user.id = token.sub;
      return session;
    },
  },
});
```

Use `useSession()` in components to guard routes.

---

## 8️⃣ SEO & Performance

| Technique | How |
|-----------|-----|
| **SSR / ISR** | `getServerSideProps` or `getStaticProps` + `revalidate` |
| **Image Optimization** | `<Image>` component with `next/image` |
| **Lazy Loading** | `loading="lazy"` on images, dynamic imports |
| **Code Splitting** | `next/dynamic` for heavy components |
| **Meta Tags** | `next/head` + `next-seo` |
| **Structured Data** | JSON‑LD in `<Head>` |
| **Sitemap** | `next-sitemap` package |
| **Accessibility** | ARIA roles, semantic HTML, `eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y` |

---

## 9️⃣ Testing

| Tool | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| **Jest** | Unit tests |
| **React Testing Library** | Component rendering & interaction |
| **Cypress** | E2E tests (cart flow, checkout) |
| **Storybook** | UI component library |
| **Playwright** | Cross‑browser testing |

**Example unit test (components/product/ProductCard.test.tsx)**

```tsx
import { render, screen } from '@testing-library/react';
import { ProductCard } from './ProductCard';

test('renders product title and price', () => {
  render(
    <ProductCard
      id="1"
      title="Test Product"
      price={99.99}
      imageUrl="/placeholder.png"
    />
  );
  expect(screen.getByText(/Test Product/i)).toBeInTheDocument();
  expect(screen.getByText(/\$99\.99/i)).toBeInTheDocument();
});
```

---

## 10️⃣ Deployment & CI/CD

| Platform | Why |
|----------|-----|
| **Vercel** | Native Next.js support, instant preview, edge caching |
| **Netlify** | Easy build hooks, serverless functions |
| **AWS Amplify** | Full‑stack, CI/CD, hosting |
| **Docker + Kubernetes** | For custom hosting or micro‑services |

**Sample GitHub Actions workflow (`.github/workflows/deploy.yml`)**

```yaml
name: Deploy to Vercel

on:
  push:
    branches: [main]

jobs:
  deploy:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v3
      - uses: amondnet/vercel-action@v20
        with:
          vercel-token: ${{ secrets.VERCEL_TOKEN }}
          vercel-org-id: ${{ secrets.VERCEL_ORG_ID }}
          vercel-project-id: ${{ secrets.VERCEL_PROJECT_ID }}
          vercel-args: '--prod'
```

---

## 11️⃣ Checklist Before Launch

- [ ] **Responsive design** – mobile‑first, breakpoints tested
- [ ] **Accessibility audit** – Lighthouse, axe-core
- [ ] **Performance audit** – Lighthouse, bundle size < 200 KB
- [ ] **SEO** – meta tags, structured data, sitemap
- [ ] **Security** – HTTPS, CSP, XSS protection
- [ ] **Analytics** – Google Analytics / Plausible
- [ ] **Error monitoring** – Sentry
- [ ] **Backup** – database snapshots
- [ ] **Documentation** – README, component docs

